# Window-relation certificate for Pico KoalaBear

Data and kernel checks for the middle bound of `WideTrail.Poseidon2.PicoKoalaBear`, used in
`WideTrail.Poseidon2.PicoKoalaBearMiddle`. The partial-round matrix is `diag d + J` over
`ZMod 2130706433` with
the Pico diagonal `d = PicoKoalaBear.diag`,
the S-box on coordinate `0`, and the window is the `20` partial rounds.

* `diagonal`: the entries of `d` as canonical representatives.
* `psi`, `gamma`: a chain of length `16` (`WideTrail.Hades.WindowRelation`). It gives one linear
  relation between the S-box differences of any `17` consecutive partial rounds; the four
  relations of the window start at the rounds `0`, `1`, `2` and `3`.
* `singles`, `pairs`: for each of the `20` patterns of one active round and the `190` patterns of
  two active rounds among `0, …, 19`, a combination of the four relations that, restricted to the
  variables of the pattern, is one variable of the pattern.
* `trailStates`, `trailOutputs`: a trail through the `20` rounds whose active rounds are exactly
  `0`, `2` and `4`.

`relations_check` and `trail_check` evaluate `Hades.RelationCheck.checkAll` and
`Hades.RelationCheck.checkTrail` on these lists by `decide +kernel`. The data were computed
outside Lean from the literals of the instance file; nothing depends on how they were found,
since the checks are complete. This file imports only `WideTrail.Hades.RelationCheck`, which
imports only `Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic`.

## What is not claimed

The checks are statements about lists of natural numbers. What they mean for trails is proved in
`WideTrail.Hades.WindowRelation` and applied in `WideTrail.Poseidon2.PicoKoalaBearMiddle`.
-/

